WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.960
A devastating discovery has been made in&nbsp;
Canada: the remains of 215 children have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.760
been found buried at the site of a former&nbsp;
boarding school for indigenous students.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.560
The school in British Columbia was part of a&nbsp;
nationwide scheme that took in First Nations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.080
children, in an effort to assimilate them into&nbsp;
Canadian society. Investigations have shown there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.440
was widespread abuse. These latest findings are&nbsp;
once again opening a wound that has yet to heal.&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.000
Row upon row of children's shoes – each&nbsp;
pair marking a lost son or daughter.&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.600
In Vancouver, people gathered to mourn the&nbsp;
215 children whose remains were found at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.120
a former Indigenous residential&nbsp;
school, with ground-penetrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.920
radar confirming the grim discovery.
"It was shocking at every single level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:57.840
And you know right now you know our community&nbsp;
is grieving. We all had to take time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:06.320
absorb what we were told, what we'd seen. And, you&nbsp;
know, we're still grappling through the effects."&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:13.280
Founded in 1890, the Kamloops school was one of&nbsp;
Canada's state-run Indigenous residential schools.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.360
After being forcibly separated from their parents,&nbsp;
children were made to convert to Christianity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.800
and banned from speaking their native languages.&nbsp;
Physical and sexual abuse by headmasters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:31.760
teachers was common -- a 2015 report found that&nbsp;
over 3,200 children had died from maltreatment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:38.720
neglect in what it called a "cultural genocide."
The Kamloops school closed in 1978 – but rumors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.840
persisted that the deaths of many children had&nbsp;
been covered up. Canada's politicians – including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.600
Prime Minister Justin Trudeau – said&nbsp;
they were heartbroken by the news.&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.480
"There's nothing more painful&nbsp;
in life than losing a child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.840
My heart breaks today thinking of all the loving&nbsp;
parents who never saw their children return home."&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.440
The Tk'emlups te Secwepemc tribe says it&nbsp;
is working with the coroner and museums&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.840
to try to shed light on the grim discovery&nbsp;
– and find records of the children's deaths.

